So far, we have modeled the functional levels of individual subsystems and derived the probability density function of the time of failure and the expression for the hazard function. In this section, we construct a model for human mortality by considering humans as a collection of subsystems. When the functional level of a subsystem declines and fails, the remaining subsystems experience increased load, leading to accelerated failure and eventual death. If even one out of the n subsystems fails, we consider it as the death of an individual, i.e., a human. Assuming the probability variables for the time of failure of each of the n subsystems as \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
